#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064342 :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ca2c1b-08ce-5224-a752-7911554c06e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234755}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234755} :answer-field/id #uuid "616098ac-de92-57f7-a966-f500d556595b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "840e39fc-48e8-52c6-b612-48460181a806" :question/math-academy-id "q-167637" :question/problem "Find $m,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=k(x)$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n$m=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have $k(x)=3{e}^{x}-{x}^{3}-2x.$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is equal to ${k}^{′}(0).$ From step 6, the derivative is\n\n$$\n{k}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{x}-3{x}^{2}-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=0$ and get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{′}(0) & =3{e}^{0}-3(0)^{2}-2 \\\\  & =3-0-2 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $1.$" :step/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235730 :multistep/_steps {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235301 :multistep/id #uuid "8fd21532-89f6-5c25-a765-13883174e1e0"}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064342 :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a4859e2-30ff-519a-9a6c-35af3d551f32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510701}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510701} :answer-field/id #uuid "d52995ac-26e6-5baf-863a-2d28b3cb00b8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "23f74b85-e755-53c7-b42c-a010cf3710be" :question/problem "Find $m,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=k(x)$ at the point where $x=0.$\n\nWe have $k(x)=-x^{3} -5 x + 5 e^{x}$ and $k^{\\prime}(x)=-3 x^{2} + 5 e^{x} -5.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have $k(x)=-x^{3} -5 x + 5 e^{x}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is equal to $k^{\\prime}(0).$ The given derivative is\n\n$$\nk^{\\prime}(x)=-3 x^{2} + 5 e^{x} -5.\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=0$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k^{\\prime}(0) & =-3 (0)^{2} + 5 e^{(0)} -5 \\\\ & =-5+0+5 \\\\ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $0.$"}]}
